The '''1997 UEFA Super Cup''' was a two-legged [[Association football|football]] match played on 8 January 1998 and 11 March 1998 between [[Borussia Dortmund]] of Germany, winner of the [[1996–97 UEFA Champions League]], and [[FC Barcelona|Barcelona]] of Spain, winner of the [[1996–97 UEFA Cup Winners' Cup]]. Barcelona won the match 3–1 on aggregate, beating Borussia Dortmund 2–0 at [[Camp Nou]] in the first leg and drawing the second leg 1–1 in [[Westfalenstadion]], [[Dortmund]].

This was the last Super Cup played over two legs. Since 1998, it has been played as a single match at a neutral venue.

